[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105629,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "<p><em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em>-rearranged fibroblastic tumour is a benign, locally recurring fibroblastic tumour with a characteristic clinical, morphological, immunohistochemical, and genetic profile.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-16T11:48:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105630,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "<p >8810/0 <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em>-rearranged fibroblastic tumour</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-16T11:46:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105631,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F7C Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105632,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> acral fibroblastic spindle cell neoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105633,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105634,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "<p><em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em>-rearranged fibroblastic tumours occur in the dermis and subcutis of the distal extremities, mainly in acral sites {29309308; 29957732}. One bone tumour, located in the tibia, has been reported so far {32710151}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-16T11:49:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105635,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a superficially located, often slow-growing lesion at the distal extremities, mainly in acral sites {29309308; 29957732}. The tumour in the tibia caused pain and diffuse swelling {32710151}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105636,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a strong female preponderance. Patient ages range from 1&nbsp;to 70&nbsp;years, with two lesions described in children so far {29309308; 29957732}. The neoplasm of the tibia was in an adult {32710151}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105637,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105638,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumorigenesis is driven by <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em> fusion, resulting from a t(15;22)(q22.33;q12.2) translocation. SMAD3, a transcriptional regulator, is involved in the TGF-&beta;/SMAD signalling pathway for fibroblasts producing extracellular matrix proteins. <em>FN1</em> mRNA upregulation is similar to that in other fibroblastic tumours. ERG overexpression appears to be unique to this tumour type and is not seen in other paediatric fibroblastic lesions {29309308; 29957732}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105639,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "<p><em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em>-rearranged fibroblastic tumours are relatively circumscribed nodular or multinodular lesions with a white-grey cut surface {29957732}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-16T11:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105640,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions are located in the dermis and subcutis. They show a nodular or multinodular growth pattern with infiltrative margins. There is commonly a biphasic appearance, with high cellularity at the periphery and variable central hyalinization. The spindle cells are arranged in intersecting fascicles. Nuclei are monomorphic and elongated. The cytoplasm is inconspicuous. Calcification may occur in the hyalinized areas, possibly as a sign of a longstanding lesion. ERG expression is a consistent immunohistochemical finding, unlike in other fibroblastic lesions, and other markers are negative (CD34, SMA, desmin, caldesmon, S100, SOX10, MUC4, &beta;-catenin) {29309308; 29957732}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105641,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105642,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of a fusion of <em>EWSR1</em> (exon&nbsp;7) with <em>SMAD3</em> (exon&nbsp;5), usually by RT-PCR, next-generation sequencing techniques, or FISH (the latter commonly for <em>EWSR1</em>), is required for diagnosis {29309308; 29957732}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105643,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a superficially located infiltrating tumour, commonly in the distal extremities&nbsp;/ acral sites, consisting of monomorphic spindle cells with central hyalinization; nuclear ERG expression; detection of an <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em> fusion gene.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105644,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is not clinically relevant as far as we know, because this lesion is at worst locally aggressive {29309308; 29957732}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105645,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 153,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrence has been described in 60% of the soft tissue cases and occurs after incomplete excision. The prognosis is excellent {29309308; 29957732; 32710151}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:45:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]